    "body": "# What does this PR do ?\n\nFixes #6453: under sequence parallelism, adapters on `TELayerNormColumnParallelLinear` (LoRA, DoRA, CanonicalLoRA) lost their part of the input gradient. This PR stops using TE's gathered LayerNorm output so the gradient is kept.\n\n# Changelog\n\n- `peft/utils.py`: `get_adapter_attributes_from_linear` now always sets `return_layernorm_output_gathered = False`. TE's `LayerNormLinear` backward drops the gradient of a gathered LayerNorm output, so the adapter's input-gradient term was never added.\n- `peft/utils.py`: removed the block that set `disable_sequence_parallel_comm = True`. The adapter now gets only its local slice of the sequence and does its own all-gather. In the backward pass, that gather sends the adapter's gradient back into the input gradient.\n- `peft/utils.py`: removed the `packaging` and `importlib.metadata.version` imports, which only that block used.\n- `peft/utils.py`: added a docstring note that `sequence_parallel_input_regather` no longer changes this function's output. The argument is kept so existing callers don't break.\n- `peft/utils.py`: added a TODO to bring back the gathered-output path once TE adds the missing gradient.\n- `tests/unit_tests/peft/test_utils.py`: the default path now expects `return_layernorm_output_gathered=False` and `disable_sequence_parallel_comm=False`. Removed the TE version patch the test no longer needs.\n- Cost: one extra all-gather in forward and one extra reduce-scatter in backward for each adapted layer.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
